From 2cdac55c30f1dd8eedf8b3f38f82dfea879ffda9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openrazer-win contributor <contributor@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:14:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Studio: devices and batteries in the tray, tray names,
 low-battery warning

The tray icon's tooltip lists each device on its own line with its
battery (and "charging"), and the menu shows the same lines, greyed,
above Open, Restart and Quit. Each device can be given a name for the
tray in Settings > System tray (empty: its own name; nowhere else
changes).

A Windows notification announces a low battery once per discharge:
at or below a level (15 % by default) and again only after the device
has charged to a second level (25 %) or is charging. Both levels, and
the warning itself, are set in Settings > System tray. Shown with the
Shell notify-icon balloon through windows-sys, no new dependency.
